Run from this directory:

    kanso test m

m/m.kso declares `type found` with two fields; m/m_test.kso declares
`fn found a b`. Put in the same file, the two are refused with "the name
`found` is already taken". Split between a module file and its test file,
nothing is reported and every call to `found` with two arguments builds the
record. In the regex port this turned 21 tests red at once with messages
that showed records where strings were expected.
